This directory is vendored from choudoufu
(https://github.com/INTENTIUS/choudoufu), pkg/identity, at commit
9807fdc1fa595e6d425cc541e8d43d48f43dde6e (branch integration/choudoufu-engine).

Every .go file here is covered by the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0,
file by file, as its own header says (SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0). The
MPL text is at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. The rest of this repository is
Apache-2.0; MPL-2.0 is file-level, so the two sit side by side and nothing
outside this directory takes on the MPL.

Files carried unchanged: every non-test .go file of pkg/identity.

Not carried: every _test.go file.

Why vendored rather than required: plunge was asked to import
github.com/intentius/choudoufu/pkg/identity at 9807fdc1fa. Requiring it means
requiring the whole choudoufu module, whose go.mod declares go 1.27.1 (this
tree builds with go 1.26.6) and pulls OpenTofu's dependency graph into
pkg/go.mod, where minimal version selection would raise versions shared with
Pulumi's own dependencies. pkg/identity imports only the standard library, so
it is copied whole instead. A later choudoufu change to it is a re-copy of
this directory at the new commit.
